### Non-Chartered Items

#### 6. YANG Path Format (ypath)
* **Presentation:** [6. YANG path format (ypath)](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-netconf-yang-path-format-ypath-00) (presented by Rob Wilton)
* **Discussion Points:**
  - Presented for information (FYI); primary draft home is the NETMOD Working Group.
  - Defines a simplified, JSON-like path format covering schema paths, instance data paths, and filter paths for YANG Push v2 and YANG Packages.
  - Per Andersson noted similarities to RESTCONF data resource URI paths. Kent Watsen and Rob Wilton discussed keeping the YPath document abstract in NETMOD while documenting protocol-specific applications within NETCONF/RESTCONF drafts.

#### 7. Comparable Sequence Numbers Across Publishers in YANG Datastore Telemetry
* **Presentation:** [7. Comparable Sequence Numbers Across Publishers in YANG Datastore Telemetry](https://datatracker.ietf.org/meeting/127/materials/slides-127-netconf-7-comparable-sequence-numbers-across-publishers-in-yang-datastore-telemetry-01) (presented by Syam Kumar)
* **Discussion Points:**
  - Proposed a Hybrid Logical Clock (HLC) mechanism (combining physical timestamps with a logical tiebreaker) to resolve message ordering and wraparound issues across distributed telemetry publishers.
  - Rob Wilton expressed strong reservations against including HLC in core `draft-ietf-netconf-yang-push-2` due to high implementation cost and inter-publisher IPC coordination overhead. Syam Kumar agreed to follow up with details on the mailing list.

